{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-74166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the denominator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-74166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaff6e11a7271134ca3a9345b7a0aa36fd113ba17aea261898867c9183a72f7"} {"question" "q-74166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-74166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-74166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1}=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1)}}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1)}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaff6e11a7271134ca3a9345b7a0aa36fd113ba17aea261898867c9183a72f7"} {"question" "q-120657" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120657" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120657" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to $({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)^{2}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)^{2}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1=({sec}^{2}⁡x)^{2}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use simplify our expression and use $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({sec}^{2}⁡x)^{2}-2\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1+{1}^{2} & =({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)^{2} \\\\  & =({tan}^{2}⁡x)^{2} \\\\  & ={tan}^{4}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)^{2}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1={tan}^{4}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaff6e11a7271134ca3a9345b7a0aa36fd113ba17aea261898867c9183a72f7"} {"question" "q-120806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1"] ["math" "2{tan}^{4}⁡x+1"] ["math" "{tan}^{4}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{tan}^{4}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify and use $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/state.json" "file_sha256" "9650be98f8c0626b876ebf39f31e0fe29f3f7519959a7f432b0f23766b3f052c"} {"question" "q-120808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039530/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaff6e11a7271134ca3a9345b7a0aa36fd113ba17aea261898867c9183a72f7"} {"question" "q-120808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1403